 
* breseq -l/--limit-fold-coverage now keeps reads (or read pairs) at even
  intervals through the input, where it used to take reads from the start until
  it had enough. Reads deposited from an aligned BAM come back sorted by
  reference position, so the old behavior covered only the start of the genome
  at the requested depth and left the rest with none. The fraction kept is the
  bases wanted divided by the bases in all of the read files, estimated from
  the start of each file so the input is still read once; the coverage achieved
  is therefore approximate. With several read files the subset is now taken
  from all of them, where later files used to be skipped once the limit was
  reached. Nothing is random: the same input and limit always give the same
  reads. Read names still number reads by their position in the input.
* gdtools FILTER/REMOVE: new -I/--clear-ids option, which writes a dot (.) in
  the id and parent-ids columns of the entries that remain, so that editing a
  GenomeDiff file does not renumber every entry after the change. Conditions
  (-c) are now optional when this option is given. It is refused together with
  --renumber, and for files with 'before' or 'within' fields, whose values are
  entry ids. Validation entries (CURA, TSEQ, PFGE, ...) are removed along with
  the evidence, since an id was all that tied them to a mutation.
